Palette/table provenance

Applies to huc6260_yuv.hex and huc6260_yuv.mif: the extracted 512-entry
HuC6260 digital table, transcribed via pbpry_int_lut and index_lut in
Kitrinx/TG16_Palette bfbii.h at commit
 e8cdf400f970753ccdf5c17446b5b62eead66e0f.
https://github.com/Kitrinx/TG16_Palette/blob/e8cdf400f970753ccdf5c17446b5b62eead66e0f/bfbii.h

The RGB capture array bfbii_lut is not the extracted digital ROM table.
Calibration follows tg16color.c at the same commit. bfbii.h has no separate
notice; the complete MIT notice below is preserved from tg16color.c.
https://github.com/Kitrinx/TG16_Palette/blob/e8cdf400f970753ccdf5c17446b5b62eead66e0f/tg16color.c

Furrtek supplied the primary test-mode readout evidence; this notice credits
the supporting Kitrinx transcription/calibration software, without asserting
a separate licence grant for Furrtek's photographs or article.

